This establishes a serial communication channel. You can use standard input/output (stdio) 
or Python's pyserial library on the Raspberry Pi to send and receive data 
from a program running on the V5 Brain.

GPIO pins
RS-485
Serial Communication
Modbus RTU, BACnet, or Profibus

Data format: Start bit, data, stop bit
Asynchronous (Baud Rate)
Half-Duplex or Full-duplex

